## Run it

```bash
make build
./bin/{{project_slug}}            # full-screen UI in a terminal
./bin/{{project_slug}} --no-tui   # the same tasks as text
./bin/{{project_slug}} --json     # the same tasks as JSON
```

In the UI: `↑`/`↓` or `j`/`k` move, `/` filters, `enter` opens, `esc` goes back, `q` quits, `?` shows every key. When stdin or stdout isn't a terminal (a pipe, CI, an editor's task runner) it prints the text list instead of starting the UI.

